{"id": "md-story", "type": "visualization", "attributes": {"title": "About this dashboard", "description": "", "uiStateJSON": "{}", "kibanaSavedObjectMeta": {"searchSourceJSON": "{\"query\": {\"query\": \"\", \"language\": \"kuery\"}, \"filter\": []}"}, "visState": "{\"title\": \"About this dashboard\", \"type\": \"markdown\", \"aggs\": [], \"params\": {\"fontSize\": 11, \"openLinksInNewTab\": true, \"markdown\": \"**Confluent SIEM optimization**\\n\\nZeek network logs and syslog stream from the laptop into **Confluent Cloud** (Fluent Bit). **Flink SQL** normalizes every event, then forwards only security-relevant ones to Elastic - **filtered**, **enriched** with threat intel and the asset inventory, and **PII-masked** (`user.name` is a salted hash, e-mails are redacted).\\n\\nThe **full, unfiltered copy** of every log line is kept as **Apache Iceberg** tables by **Tableflow** (Confluent-managed storage) - for forensics, compliance and analytics at object-storage cost.\\n\\n[Open all SIEM events in Discover](/app/discover#/view/search-siem?_g=(time:(from:now-1h,to:now)))\"}}"}, "references": [], "coreMigrationVersion": "8.8.0", "typeMigrationVersion": "8.5.0"}
{"id": "md-pii", "type": "visualization", "attributes": {"title": "Check PII masking", "description": "", "uiStateJSON": "{}", "kibanaSavedObjectMeta": {"searchSourceJSON": "{\"query\": {\"query\": \"\", \"language\": \"kuery\"}, \"filter\": []}"}, "visState": "{\"title\": \"Check PII masking\", \"type\": \"markdown\", \"aggs\": [], \"params\": {\"fontSize\": 11, \"openLinksInNewTab\": true, \"markdown\": \"**[Open the PII masking check in Discover](/app/discover#/view/search-pii?_g=(time:(from:now-1h,to:now)))**\\n\\nFlink masks personal data *before* it leaves Confluent Cloud - the SIEM never stores it:\\n\\n| Field | Masked as |\\n|---|---|\\n| `user.name` | `user-` + 12 hex chars (salted SHA-256, same user = same value) |\\n| `message` - user names | `[USER]` |\\n| `message`, `url.original` - e-mails | `[EMAIL]` |\\n\\nExample: `Failed password for [USER] from 203.0.113.66 port 51234 ssh2`\\n\\n**Pass:** no real name or e-mail address in the table on the right.\\n\\nSearch tips: `user.name : user-*` - `message : EMAIL`. Kibana's word search ignores brackets, so look for `[USER]` in the message column.\\n\\nThe unmasked originals stay in the Iceberg lake: `./scripts/03-lake-query.sh`.\"}}"}, "references": [], "coreMigrationVersion": "8.8.0", "typeMigrationVersion": "8.5.0"}
